  "_about": "an olive baboon SCULPTED on its rig (2026-11-05, gen: scratchpad sc/prim/gen/baboon.py, written in its standing pose): a male Old World monkey walking on its palms and soles, flat fingers and toes forward, the limbs long and even; a dog's long dark MUZZLE with the nostrils at its very end, the eyes deep under a heavy brow, pale upper lids, small ears; olive ticked fur (agouti) and the male's MANE a cape over the shoulders and neck (shag); bare grey callosities on the buttocks under the BROKEN tail -- carried up and back off the rump for a third of its length, then hanging straight down (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): small flat shells with a point at the top (sharp.js `fin`), close to the head, the hollow out and forward; the roots faired. (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/tails.py) The TAIL is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along its bones, not a chain of cones blended one into the next: no beads, its thin end exact rings. (`thin` 3 set by hand: under 3 cells across it is drawn as rings, the tip rounded.)",
